WEBVTT

00:10.510 --> 00:11.761
Damned bugs!

00:11.845 --> 00:16.099
It's because you're all holed up
in your nests cozily

00:16.182 --> 00:19.811
that those incompetent adventurers
can't clear the dungeon,

00:19.894 --> 00:22.230
forcing me to keep

00:23.440 --> 00:26.443
working overtime!

00:27.902 --> 00:30.655
An arachne in its nest
is incredibly hard to deal with!

00:31.781 --> 00:32.824
Though it's probably too late to say that.

00:32.907 --> 00:37.203
She broke the dungeon wall
and went straight to the boss' room.

00:37.287 --> 00:39.914
I didn't know there was such a strategy.

00:40.707 --> 00:42.584
At this rate, we'll be shorthanded,

00:42.667 --> 00:47.213
and I won't be able
to join the newcomer training!

00:50.258 --> 00:51.926
Newcomer training?

00:52.010 --> 00:54.387
For the sake of clocking out on time,

00:54.471 --> 00:56.806
die!

01:01.102 --> 01:04.397
All you incompetent adventurers

01:04.481 --> 01:07.358
and bosses, die!

01:07.901 --> 01:09.235
I'll kill you all!

01:14.491 --> 01:17.827
I MAY BE A GUILD RECEPTIONIST, BUT
I'LL SOLO ANY BOSS TO CLOCK OUT ON TIME

02:40.618 --> 02:42.203
To think that even the arachne

02:42.287 --> 02:45.331
would be defeated by a receptionist
who wanted to attend training,

02:45.415 --> 02:48.251
I don't think any of us
could have imagined that.

02:48.334 --> 02:52.881
But Ms. Alina, do you really need
to attend the newcomer training?

02:52.964 --> 02:57.552
It's to get overtime
out of my life for good.

03:00.179 --> 03:02.265
Iffole Counter's overtime hours

03:02.348 --> 03:05.435
are much higher
than those of other counters.

03:05.518 --> 03:07.854
So we received a warning
from the Guild headquarters.

03:08.479 --> 03:11.900
And they've been promoting
workplace reform in recent years.

03:11.983 --> 03:14.986
<i>That's just an idealistic theory.</i>

03:15.069 --> 03:18.948
That's why
I've talked to HR at the headquarters

03:19.032 --> 03:21.034
about ways to reduce overtime hours.

03:21.117 --> 03:23.995
In the end, they came up
with a special solution.

03:24.078 --> 03:25.371
<i>Finally...</i>

03:25.455 --> 03:29.167
<i>Finally, they're going to increase
the number of receptionists.</i>

03:29.250 --> 03:32.795
The one who proposes the most efficient
business betterment plan

03:32.879 --> 03:35.381
will get a birthday leave.

03:37.091 --> 03:40.303
That's not right.

03:40.386 --> 03:44.265
But I do want a birthday leave.

03:44.349 --> 03:46.142
That's true.

03:46.226 --> 03:49.729
Every year, it's only
while working overtime that I realize,

03:49.812 --> 03:52.065
"Oh, it's my birthday today."

03:52.899 --> 03:55.777
- What about your birthday celebration?
- I just go home, wash up, and sleep.

03:56.736 --> 03:57.862
Ms. Alina.

03:57.946 --> 04:00.281
No matter how you look at it,
that kind of life is way too boring.

04:00.365 --> 04:04.702
<i>The Guild Master promised
to increase the number of receptionists,</i>

04:04.786 --> 04:07.413
<i>but it will take some time before
the personnel changes are announced.</i>

04:08.164 --> 04:10.667
<i>I really want this birthday leave.</i>

04:10.750 --> 04:13.503
A business betterment plan?

04:13.586 --> 04:17.674
- I have no idea.
- Don't worry. I feel the same.

04:18.424 --> 04:20.885
By the way, what have you been looking at?

04:20.969 --> 04:23.429
Materials for the newcomer training.

04:24.013 --> 04:26.432
That's... Let me see.

04:27.767 --> 04:30.436
"Instructor, Rosetta Rhuberry."

04:30.520 --> 04:32.605
That's right.

04:32.689 --> 04:35.900
She's the living legend who branded the
unremarkable and undesirable receptionist

04:35.984 --> 04:39.279
and turned it
into a super popular profession.

04:40.238 --> 04:41.990
<i>Not only did she introduce cute uniforms,</i>

04:42.073 --> 04:44.909
<i>but she also proposed learning customer
service etiquette and developed a manual.</i>

04:44.993 --> 04:48.288
<i>It wouldn't be an exaggeration
to say that she laid the groundwork</i>

04:48.371 --> 04:50.415
<i>for the current receptionists.</i>

04:50.915 --> 04:52.166
And she's the author

04:52.250 --> 04:55.920
of the bestseller "If You Want
to Be a Receptionist, Eat Beans."

04:56.004 --> 04:56.921
It's my favorite book...

04:57.005 --> 04:58.840
- Those aren't important.
- Not important?

04:58.923 --> 05:03.094
What's really amazing about her
is her administrative skills.

05:03.761 --> 05:07.932
<i>One time, three new dungeons appeared,
and adventurers all went to the office.</i>

05:08.016 --> 05:10.560
<i>But she was able to handle
all the requests on her own.</i>

05:11.311 --> 05:14.939
What? That's not something
a human could achieve.

05:15.023 --> 05:19.319
If I could learn the secret of her superb
administrative skills from her,

05:20.194 --> 05:21.863
forget about the birthday leave,

05:21.946 --> 05:25.283
I’d never have to work overtime again!

05:25.366 --> 05:28.328
But haven't we been
working overtime lately

05:28.411 --> 05:31.205
because they just discovered
a huge dungeon?

05:31.289 --> 05:33.750
I don't know
if the Counter Manager will let us go.

05:34.375 --> 05:37.754
It'll be fine as long as we remove
the cause of our current overtime.

05:39.088 --> 05:41.799
Is that why you're here
to get rid of the boss?

05:41.883 --> 05:44.385
By the way, Ms. Alina.
When is your birthday?

05:44.469 --> 05:45.970
I'm not telling you.

05:46.929 --> 05:47.972
I thought so.

05:48.056 --> 05:49.640
For this year's training,

05:49.724 --> 05:52.977
Silver Sword will be participating
as instructors for the demo battle.

05:54.604 --> 05:56.147
Will Jade be there too?

05:56.814 --> 05:58.024
Ms. Alina.

05:58.107 --> 06:01.736
Could you not make that disgusted face
like you're about to work overtime?

06:01.819 --> 06:03.613
A stalker like you

06:03.696 --> 06:07.366
would stand at the back of the classroom
and stare at me the whole time, right?

06:08.910 --> 06:11.871
Indeed,
the old me probably would've done that.

06:11.954 --> 06:14.290
But I've realized something.

06:14.373 --> 06:16.334
In order to get Ms. Alina to look at me,

06:16.417 --> 06:19.087
I have to change the way I act.

06:19.170 --> 06:20.254
From now on,

06:20.338 --> 06:23.591
I'll only do things that
will make you like me, Ms. Alina.

06:23.674 --> 06:27.553
I call it an "Image Improvement Campaign"!

06:27.637 --> 06:30.389
Then, just breathe quietly
for the rest of your life.

06:30.473 --> 06:32.558
That's the only way
to improve my impression of you.

06:33.601 --> 06:34.977
Ms. Alina.

06:35.061 --> 06:37.563
The training is for three days
and two nights.

06:37.647 --> 06:40.316
If you do anything weird,
I won't forgive you.

06:40.399 --> 06:42.360
Yes, leave it to me.

06:42.443 --> 06:45.029
I'll definitely make you see me
in a different light!

06:45.113 --> 06:46.572
Does the Leader's romance

06:46.656 --> 06:49.408
really have to start with being recognized
as an ordinary human?

06:49.492 --> 06:51.661
It seems like a long way to go.

06:53.955 --> 06:55.665
It's huge!

06:55.748 --> 06:58.376
I feel like I'll get lost if I come alone.

06:58.459 --> 06:59.544
If you mess up at work,

06:59.627 --> 07:01.212
you'll be called here
even if you don't want to.

07:01.295 --> 07:03.131
You'll remember it someday.

07:04.090 --> 07:08.136
Ms. Alina.
You've been here many times, haven't you?

07:09.137 --> 07:14.392
I'm sure you all know that the Guild
headquarters used to be a dungeon too.

07:14.475 --> 07:16.144
Fifteen years ago,

07:16.227 --> 07:19.355
the Silver Sword from two generations ago

07:19.439 --> 07:23.359
successfully cleared
this S-rank dungeon, Fortress of Ash.

07:24.277 --> 07:26.821
The receptionists are so cute!

07:26.904 --> 07:27.947
They're like angels!

07:28.030 --> 07:30.032
Which girl do you like?

07:30.116 --> 07:32.452
The girl with green eyes and black hair.

07:32.535 --> 07:34.662
She looks so pure and delicate.

07:34.745 --> 07:36.831
It makes me want to protect her.

07:37.540 --> 07:38.958
I wonder if she has a boyfriend.

07:39.625 --> 07:42.628
<i>Hearing people look at Ms. Alina that way</i>

07:42.712 --> 07:44.255
<i>really pisses me off.</i>

07:44.338 --> 07:47.592
<i>No. I'm still in the middle
of my Image Improvement Campaign.</i>

07:47.675 --> 07:49.218
<i>I can't scold those guys here.</i>

07:49.302 --> 07:52.930
<i>I can't talk to Ms. Alina
in front of everyone either.</i>

07:53.973 --> 07:56.684
<i>But I'll remember their faces first.</i>

07:58.227 --> 08:00.229
They are the current guild master,

08:00.313 --> 08:02.648
Glen Garia's party members.

08:02.732 --> 08:05.902
As the Silver Sword
from two generations ago,

08:06.486 --> 08:10.323
they risked their lives
to conquer this Fortress of Ash.

08:10.948 --> 08:12.617
Hey, miss.

08:13.743 --> 08:16.662
You helped me again the other day.

08:17.455 --> 08:21.250
<i>Everyone came back alive
all thanks to your help.</i>

08:23.836 --> 08:26.380
- I'd like to express my gratitude.
- Don't thank me.

08:26.964 --> 08:28.966
You promised to increase
the number of receptionists.

08:29.050 --> 08:30.885
I'm sure you'll keep your promise, right?

08:33.930 --> 08:38.267
I'll double the number of receptionists.

08:40.811 --> 08:42.647
Maybe you'll have to wait a little longer.

08:42.730 --> 08:45.525
- I've got my hands full here too.
- Wait?

08:46.192 --> 08:48.528
Overtime waits for no one.

08:50.863 --> 08:53.282
You're in charge of the Guild, right?

08:53.366 --> 08:56.285
You made a promise to me
as the person in charge, right?

08:56.369 --> 08:58.788
Please take responsibility for it!

08:58.871 --> 09:03.167
Of course, I'll take care of it
as soon as possible.

09:03.251 --> 09:05.294
You absolutely have to keep your promise!

09:05.378 --> 09:07.672
You absolutely, absolutely
cannot break your promise!

09:08.256 --> 09:09.757
I know, I know.

09:09.840 --> 09:12.260
Well then, good luck with your training.

09:13.594 --> 09:15.263
By the way, miss.

09:16.556 --> 09:18.641
I'll be counting on you again next time.

09:18.724 --> 09:20.268
Next time?

09:20.351 --> 09:23.312
Dark gods like that can't
come out one after another.

09:23.396 --> 09:24.647
There won't be a next time.

09:26.440 --> 09:27.858
You're right.

09:30.903 --> 09:35.575
After that,
Glen Garia took over as guild master.

09:35.658 --> 09:40.413
Now, we're going to watch
a demo battle by the Silver Sword.

09:42.623 --> 09:43.583
Everyone.

09:43.666 --> 09:46.377
Please don't forget your dignity
as a receptionist

09:46.460 --> 09:48.379
and watch the demo battle with poise!

10:01.225 --> 10:03.519
Lord Jade!

10:03.603 --> 10:05.021
I'll root for you forever!

10:05.104 --> 10:07.982
He's so handsome in person!
I can't take it, I'm dying!

10:08.065 --> 10:10.943
Excuse me! Someone's fainted!

10:11.027 --> 10:14.405
As an Executioner stan,
I can't lose either!

10:14.488 --> 10:17.491
I have to make my own cheering fan too!

10:18.492 --> 10:20.494
All new receptionists,

10:20.578 --> 10:22.496
welcome to the Guild headquarters.

10:23.122 --> 10:26.500
I'm the leader of Silver Sword,
Jade Scrade.

10:28.586 --> 10:31.047
I'm glad to see you all in high spirits.

10:36.052 --> 10:39.221
<i>Don't tell me he's going to call me</i>

10:39.305 --> 10:42.391
<i>"Ms. Alina" in front of everyone?</i>

10:42.475 --> 10:46.604
<i>Don't call me that!</i>

10:50.983 --> 10:53.069
Any questions?

10:53.152 --> 10:55.488
- Me!
- Do you have a girlfriend?

10:55.571 --> 10:58.199
- What's your type?
- Everyone!

10:58.282 --> 11:00.618
Please don't forget your dignity
as a receptionist.

11:02.995 --> 11:04.997
<i>I almost forgot about
his Image Improvement Campaign.</i>

11:05.081 --> 11:07.208
<i>So is that why he didn't
act friendly like usual</i>

11:07.291 --> 11:09.710
<i>and intentionally kept his distance?</i>

11:10.461 --> 11:13.005
<i>For Jade,
this idea is actually pretty good.</i>

11:13.089 --> 11:14.715
<i>Finally, he's not pestering me
for no reason.</i>

11:14.799 --> 11:16.092
<i>I feel more at ease.</i>

11:25.559 --> 11:28.062
This... this is the training building.

11:28.145 --> 11:29.313
It's so old.

11:29.397 --> 11:31.816
Is that all you can say, Ms. Alina?

11:32.566 --> 11:35.694
That rumor may be true, after all.

11:35.778 --> 11:36.862
Rumor?

11:36.946 --> 11:41.450
I heard that this training building
might have that "thing."

11:41.534 --> 11:42.701
Ghosts!

11:42.785 --> 11:44.995
I see. Let's go to our rooms
and get some rest.

11:45.079 --> 11:49.208
Wait a minute, Ms. Alina.

11:52.503 --> 11:55.423
Ms. Alina. Aren't you afraid of ghosts?

11:56.132 --> 11:58.050
Seems like you're not scared.

11:58.134 --> 12:00.469
Could you stop talking
to yourself over there?

12:02.054 --> 12:05.850
The training building still has
the same dungeon look from back then.

12:05.933 --> 12:08.519
It must be
because of the mysterious deaths

12:08.602 --> 12:11.355
of the renovation workers.

12:11.439 --> 12:14.024
It's definitely the spirits of those
who died here causing trouble.

12:14.108 --> 12:15.943
They probably didn't allocate
a budget for it.

12:16.026 --> 12:19.071
Please don't explain it
in such a super realistic way.

12:39.341 --> 12:41.302
It's here!

12:42.428 --> 12:45.306
The... the ghost!

12:57.818 --> 12:59.236
What? Isn't this Lululee?

12:59.320 --> 13:01.655
Please don't open the door suddenly!

13:01.739 --> 13:03.491
You startled me!

13:05.409 --> 13:09.830
Well... The higher-ups told us
to stay here too tonight.

13:09.914 --> 13:13.000
Please let me sleep
in your room, Ms. Alina!

13:14.168 --> 13:16.921
Actually, this training building

13:17.588 --> 13:19.215
has ghosts!

13:19.298 --> 13:22.218
I already heard about that just now.

13:23.552 --> 13:25.179
In the past,

13:25.262 --> 13:30.768
when the Guild headquarters was still
a dungeon called the Fortress of Ash,

13:30.851 --> 13:32.478
it was a widely spread rumor.

13:32.561 --> 13:35.856
It's said that this place
could connect to the afterlife.

13:35.940 --> 13:37.733
The afterlife?

13:37.816 --> 13:40.361
It's said that a small party
went into this dungeon,

13:41.070 --> 13:43.364
but the members who were adventuring
together suddenly disappeared.

13:44.031 --> 13:46.367
And there were no traces
of monsters attacking them.

13:46.450 --> 13:49.411
No one could find them
despite searching the whole dungeon.

13:49.495 --> 13:52.998
So, those who were left behind
made this speculation.

13:53.999 --> 13:59.505
Maybe they were taken
to the afterlife by something.

14:02.675 --> 14:09.014
Moreover, this training building
was also part of the Fortress of Ash.

14:09.848 --> 14:10.891
Even now,

14:10.975 --> 14:15.521
<i>people still claim to have seen
a mysterious silhouette in a black robe,</i>

14:15.604 --> 14:18.107
<i>or that they felt a strange aura of sorts.</i>

14:18.190 --> 14:20.651
<i>Such rumors have never ceased to exist.</i>

14:20.734 --> 14:22.903
<i>I'm sure</i>

14:22.987 --> 14:27.366
those are the spirits of adventurers
taken by the Shinigami!

14:27.449 --> 14:30.578
- No!
- I see.

14:31.745 --> 14:33.747
Aren't you scared, Ms. Alina?

14:33.831 --> 14:36.333
It's the Shinigami! It's ghosts!

14:36.417 --> 14:39.920
I'm someone
who can work overtime alone late at night.

14:40.004 --> 14:43.132
If I'm scared of that,
I won't be able to finish my work.

14:43.883 --> 14:46.093
That's very convincing.

14:47.052 --> 14:49.972
You absolutely must take
the birthday leave

14:50.055 --> 14:52.641
and let Lord Jade help you celebrate!

14:52.725 --> 14:57.730
Why do I have to go out of my way
to see Jade on my birthday?

14:57.813 --> 15:00.691
Then what are you going
to do for your birthday?

15:00.774 --> 15:05.154
Of course, I'm going to enjoy
my special birthday program!

15:05.738 --> 15:09.241
<i>First, I'm going to sleep all the way
until afternoon.</i>

15:09.325 --> 15:11.368
<i>Then I'm going to eat something light</i>

15:11.452 --> 15:13.704
<i>and continue to lounge around.</i>

15:14.288 --> 15:15.789
<i>After that, I'll go back to sleep.</i>

15:15.873 --> 15:18.167
<i>And when I'm really hungry,</i>

15:18.250 --> 15:21.378
<i>I'm going to have an amazing dinner.</i>

15:21.462 --> 15:23.923
You basically just eat and sleep.

15:24.006 --> 15:26.175
Aren't you going to do something else?

15:26.258 --> 15:30.512
Escaping the waves of a harsh society
and enjoying a comfortable break

15:30.596 --> 15:32.932
is essential for working adults!

15:33.849 --> 15:37.645
Working adults have it rough, don't they?

15:37.728 --> 15:41.690
Come to think of it,
if you take the day off for your birthday,

15:41.774 --> 15:45.444
Jade would probably find your address
and come disturb you.

15:46.862 --> 15:48.572
It's hard to say.

15:49.406 --> 15:53.911
Don't tell me
you have a fight with Lord Jade?

15:55.037 --> 15:57.831
I mean, even when he saw you today,

15:57.915 --> 16:00.125
he didn't come over to greet you at all.

16:00.709 --> 16:04.421
That's because
Jade is on his Image Improvement Campaign.

16:04.505 --> 16:07.299
What's that?
I haven't heard anything about it.

16:07.383 --> 16:09.551
He's restraining himself
from pursuing Ms. Alina.

16:09.635 --> 16:12.680
At the same time, he can't take
the initiative to talk to her either.

16:12.763 --> 16:15.599
Thanks to that,
I'm living an extremely carefree life.

16:15.683 --> 16:20.354
You say that,
but you're actually lonely, aren't you?

16:20.437 --> 16:21.480
Not at all.

16:26.527 --> 16:27.820
That's right.

16:28.529 --> 16:32.825
We just went back to the appropriate
distance between an adventurer

16:32.908 --> 16:34.326
and a receptionist. That's all.

16:34.910 --> 16:38.497
But you like Jade a little, don't you?

16:38.580 --> 16:39.623
No.

16:41.125 --> 16:44.545
I want to hear more love stories!

16:44.628 --> 16:46.255
Well then, Ms. Laila.

16:46.338 --> 16:48.173
Do you have someone you like?

16:48.257 --> 16:49.883
Are you willing to listen to me?

16:51.218 --> 16:54.888
The one I stan the most is...

16:54.972 --> 16:56.640
Lord Executioner!

16:57.808 --> 16:59.768
His identity is unknown.
He shows up out of nowhere.

16:59.852 --> 17:01.520
And he's insanely strong.

17:01.603 --> 17:04.773
The other day, he broke through the wall
and cleared that huge dungeon.

17:04.857 --> 17:09.361
That will give me and Lord Executioner
more variety in our fantasy scenarios.

17:09.945 --> 17:11.739
For example, I was in danger
after stumbling into a dungeon.

17:11.822 --> 17:12.906
And just in the nick of time,

17:12.990 --> 17:16.118
- he came to my rescue.
- She doesn't know, does she?

17:16.201 --> 17:19.079
Or when I was about to be buried
by a crumbling wall, the Executioner

17:19.163 --> 17:21.582
- Please, don't tell her.
- protected me with his body.

17:22.833 --> 17:25.544
He's so cool!

17:25.627 --> 17:30.090
Please! Please let the Executioner
join Silver Sword!

17:30.174 --> 17:35.012
If the Executioner is willing to join us,
we'll be happy too.

17:35.095 --> 17:36.638
If we can't pull him into Silver Sword,

17:36.722 --> 17:40.225
Lord Executioner might disappear one day.

17:40.893 --> 17:42.269
Those mysterious super-strong characters

17:42.352 --> 17:45.189
always disappear
after defeating powerful enemies,

17:45.272 --> 17:48.233
saying something like,
"I've accomplished my mission."

17:48.817 --> 17:52.154
Someone mentioned it
at the Lord Executioner Study Group.

17:52.237 --> 17:55.824
It makes me so worried.

17:59.578 --> 18:02.748
This is
the information from the intel team.

18:02.831 --> 18:08.087
However, we still don't have
any new leads on the man in black.

18:08.170 --> 18:09.630
The man in black

18:10.297 --> 18:14.134
leaked the existence of secret quests
to adventurers and incited them.

18:14.218 --> 18:17.638
I'm guessing his goal
is to revive the dark gods.

18:18.180 --> 18:19.306
Leader.

18:19.973 --> 18:21.600
Do you think...

18:22.476 --> 18:23.644
there's a traitor?

18:27.189 --> 18:28.398
<i>Before this, Heitz</i>

18:28.482 --> 18:30.943
<i>stole the secret quest
from the underground library.</i>

18:31.735 --> 18:35.114
But his skill could only
be used to escape.

18:35.197 --> 18:37.449
That means he didn't use
his skill to infiltrate.

18:38.200 --> 18:41.453
Say, you should know this clearly.

18:43.247 --> 18:46.291
The people who can get him
into the underground library

18:46.375 --> 18:48.168
are only a handful.

18:52.840 --> 18:56.552
Good day, my lovely receptionists.

18:56.635 --> 19:00.139
I'm your instructor today,
Rosetta Rhuberry.

19:00.222 --> 19:01.557
It's nice to meet all of you.

19:02.224 --> 19:03.600
<i>The day has finally come.</i>

19:03.684 --> 19:07.062
<i>I must master the technique
of eliminating overtime.</i>

19:07.146 --> 19:11.316
Whether an adventurer
can get the job smoothly or not

19:11.400 --> 19:15.571
depends entirely on how a receptionist
handles the quest request.

19:15.654 --> 19:16.905
Through this lesson,

19:16.989 --> 19:21.034
I hope I can help everyone reach
the next level in their skills.

19:21.118 --> 19:24.913
<i>This is not a lesson. It's war!</i>

19:28.959 --> 19:32.171
Everyone, that's all for the first lesson.

19:32.254 --> 19:35.549
Well then, let's move on to Q&A.

19:35.632 --> 19:37.926
I have a question!

19:39.761 --> 19:42.431
Well then, the energetic lady over there.

19:42.514 --> 19:44.975
I'll get straight to the point.

19:45.058 --> 19:48.437
How can I solve the problem
of receptionists working overtime?

19:49.813 --> 19:54.443
Seems like you're not a newcomer.

19:55.110 --> 19:57.321
I've been working for three years.

19:57.404 --> 19:58.780
I see.

19:58.864 --> 20:02.576
Then, you should already know
what the reality is like.

20:03.243 --> 20:04.328
All right then.

20:04.411 --> 20:06.830
<i>I can say goodbye to working overtime now.</i>

20:06.914 --> 20:10.959
<i>And wait for the arrival
of my birthday vacation.</i>

20:11.043 --> 20:13.337
In response to your spirit,

20:13.420 --> 20:17.841
I'll teach you my secret formula
for overcoming overtime.

20:20.677 --> 20:24.181
That is to work roughly
100 overtime hours per month.

20:24.264 --> 20:26.850
Of course, that includes
working on holidays.

20:27.851 --> 20:30.479
What... what did you say?

20:30.562 --> 20:32.105
I get it.

20:32.189 --> 20:34.399
You hate working overtime, don't you?

20:34.483 --> 20:36.276
But don't worry.

20:36.360 --> 20:38.862
I have a magic to make you
not hate working overtime anymore.

20:39.905 --> 20:45.702
That is to imagine the happy faces
of your customers.

20:47.162 --> 20:48.205
What?

20:48.288 --> 20:51.959
You're suffering so much
because you see work as work.

20:52.042 --> 20:53.460
Think of work as your lover.

20:53.543 --> 20:54.836
Whether you're sleeping or awake,

20:54.920 --> 20:59.549
always think about work
and your customers' affairs.

21:02.386 --> 21:04.846
Once you reach that level,

21:04.930 --> 21:08.684
you'll be liberated
from the concept of labor

21:08.767 --> 21:12.312
and become a super receptionist.

21:13.438 --> 21:16.608
<i>She's just... She's...</i>

21:17.442 --> 21:22.823
<i>just a workaholic!</i>

21:26.159 --> 21:28.537
This way, please, Lord Jade.

21:28.620 --> 21:31.915
- Hurry!
- Ms. Alina?

21:32.916 --> 21:34.501
What happened?

21:35.168 --> 21:36.586
In class just now,

21:36.670 --> 21:40.966
she was defeated
by a near-madness workaholic aura.

21:41.591 --> 21:44.094
Workaholics are scary.

21:44.678 --> 21:46.972
Workaholics are scary.

21:48.056 --> 21:51.977
- Workaholics are scary.
- Cheer up, Ms. Alina.

21:52.686 --> 21:55.981
After all, during training,
you don't have to work overtime.

21:56.523 --> 21:57.774
Overtime?

21:59.443 --> 22:01.987
What? Oh, it's you, Jade.

22:02.696 --> 22:07.075
Now that I've seen your face,
I'm kind of relieved.

22:09.328 --> 22:10.912
Ms. Alina.

22:11.621 --> 22:13.915
Seeing my face makes you feel relieved?

22:13.999 --> 22:16.835
I thought I didn't have
to work overtime anymore.

22:16.918 --> 22:20.297
I thought I finally didn't have
to work overtime anymore.

22:20.380 --> 22:26.011
I want to go home on time!

23:58.979 --> 23:59.813
<i>Next episode.</i>

23:59.896 --> 24:02.232
<i>"Ghosts appearing during training?</i>

24:02.315 --> 24:04.901
<i>I never heard that
this kind of thing would happen!"</i>
